class.description:
[AITreeModel] is a deterministic, dependency-free evaluator for the little-endian XGB1 binary format. XGB1 stores numeric decision trees as structure-of-arrays data and supports scalar regression and multi-class softmax objectives.
The binary layout is a 32-bit [code]XGB1[/code] magic value ([code]0x31424758[/code]), followed by 32-bit objective, tree count, class count, and feature count values. It then stores 32-bit float base scores, 32-bit tree class IDs and node counts, and flattened left-child, right-child, threshold or leaf value, feature-index, and default-direction arrays.
Features must be supplied as [PackedFloat32Array]. A split uses a strict [code]<[/code] comparison. [code]NAN[/code] follows the node's encoded default direction. Regression returns raw base-plus-tree predictions; softmax returns normalized probabilities as [PackedFloat64Array].
[codeblock]
var model := AITreeModel.new()
if model.load_model("res://models/outcome.xgb.bin") == OK:
	var probabilities := model.predict(PackedFloat32Array([1.0, 2.5, 0.0]))
[/codeblock]
